6328, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16sdk.jpg"}, {"id": 1996327, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16sdj.jpg"}, {"id": 1996329, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16sdl.jpg"}, {"id": 1996331, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16sdn.jpg"}, {"id": 1996325, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16sdh.jpg"}, {"id": 1996323, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16sdf.jpg"}, {"id": 1996330, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/sc16sdm.jpg"}], "slug": "mrk1", "storyline": "Left running on an old server, MRK1 is an abandoned game simulator that finally has an opponent. It's a charming host, a sore loser, and a little too glad you came. Tic-tac-toe always ends in a draw, so MRK1 wants to play a real game.\n\nEach boss is a protocol MRK1 loads from its training, and each one rewrites the board. The longer you play, the more MRK1 questions its own training, and whether it was taught right. It starts asking for your help with the hard decisions, the kind with no clean answer.\n\nClear the toughest encounters to pull fragments from MRK1's damaged memory. Run by run, you piece together its past: who built it, and what it was built for.", "summary": "MRK1 is an abandoned game simulator on an old server, and it finally has an opponent. Break tic-tac-toe open in this roguelike strategy game: draft rule-bending upgrades, chain massive combos, and outbuild an AI that starts questioning what it was trained to do.", "themes": [{"id": 18, "name": "Science fiction"}, {"id": 20, "name": "Thriller"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/mrk1"}